            <ArticleTitle>Postprandial Endotoxemia: A Significant Contributor to Chronic Diseases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>8-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The increase of chronic diseases in the world's population continues unabated. Cardiovascular disease (CVD), type 2 diabetes (T2D), obesity, arthritis, autoimmunity, and gastrointestinal disorders are all too common and costly, and most have as their source inflammation. T2D is now considered a pandemic, and there is one commonality to many of these: They are, for the most part, preventable.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
